{
  "requirement": "TBV automatically redacts recognized credentials in source excerpts delivered\nby its inspection tools and in node text supplied to its agent requests.\nThe built-in rules replace recognized secret regions with redaction markers\nwhile preserving line breaks. SDK-supplied outline languages use the same redacted\nregions, so changing only a recognized credential does not change its\nstructural fingerprint.\n\nLoaded source snapshots retain the original text for selection and spans;\nredaction applies when preparing model-visible text and structural hashes.\nFilesystem evidence storage preserves the supplied record. Applications supply\ntheir own answer values and remain responsible for what those answers contain.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap for `requirements.sdk.sources.redaction`. Each obligation maps to a marked test with assertions that enforce it.\n\n**Redaction in delivered inspection excerpts**\n- `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[search_excerpts_redact_credentials_before_serialization_and_paging]` runs both `search_text` and `search_structure` over a file holding a GitHub token and a multi-line RSA private key.\n  - It asserts the exact redacted excerpt, with markers in place and surrounding text intact.\n  - It checks that the excerpt's line count matches the raw text.\n  - It checks that neither the token nor any key-body line appears in the serialized output.\n  - It checks that the file on disk is unchanged.\n  - It checks that the dependency recorded after `finish_search` carries the fingerprint of the unredacted snapshot.\n- `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[child_headers_use_redacted_source_when_the_language_supplies_a_header]` covers `read_node` child headers. It asserts the header shows `[REDACTED:GitHub Token]` and that the whole page text omits the token.\n\n**Redaction in node text supplied to agent requests**\n- `agent/tests.rs#fn[queued_contents_and_graph_read_tools_redact_credentials_before_delivery]` covers `contents_of_current_node` and the `read_node` tool result. It asserts the secret is absent from every request's chat history and that a redaction marker is present.\n  - The dependency fingerprint and the stored graph contents keep the original text.\n  - The credential is shown as a marker in the supplied listing only because the review tool redacts it. That is not a defect in the test.\n\n**Rules replace recognized regions with markers and preserve line breaks**\n- `redaction/tests.rs` covers the built-in rules directly:\n  - `fn[private_keys_are_redacted_from_header_through_body_keeping_lines]` checks the exact output for a private key block, including line-count equality and an embedding in Rust source.\n  - `fn[tokens_in_code_are_redacted_without_adjacent_code]` checks token redaction in code.\n  - `fn[heuristic_findings_alone_are_not_redacted]` and `fn[configuration_keys_do_not_add_sdk_specific_secret_rules]` check that unrecognized text is left alone.\n  - `fn[regions_extend_both_ways_keep_crlf_and_scan_past_a_mebibyte]` covers CRLF line breaks, region extension and large input.\n  - `fn[slices_concatenate_to_the_redacted_whole]` checks that slices join to the redacted whole.\n\n**SDK outline languages share the redacted regions, so a credential-only change keeps the structural fingerprint**\n- `outline/redaction_tests.rs#fn[hashes_do_not_depend_on_credential_values]` swaps one token for another in Rust, Markdown and plain text, and asserts the structural hashes are equal. It also asserts that a change outside the credential does change the hash, so the check is not vacuous.\n- `outline/redaction_tests.rs#fn[redaction_never_changes_an_outline]` covers YAML, Rust, TOML, Markdown and text. It asserts the outline structure is the same with and without redaction, and that the line count is preserved.\n- `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[formatted_contents_redact_credentials_while_retaining_raw_text_and_spans]` shows two sources differing only in the credential have equal fingerprints.\n\n**Snapshots keep the original text for selection and spans**\n- The same `tests/outline_content.rs` test asserts `contents.text()` equals the raw source. It also asserts a selected item's `text()` still contains the token while its `format()` is redacted.\n\n**Evidence storage preserves the supplied record**\n- `tests/storage.rs#fn[storage_preserves_completed_answers_containing_credential_shaped_text]` stores and loads an answer containing a token the scanner recognizes. It asserts the loaded output equals the stored output and that the raw record file contains the token.\n\n**Application answers** are the application's responsibility. This is a non-obligation for the SDK, and the storage test covers its observable consequence.\n\n**Not tested**\n- The generic provider-based `SourceTools` session in `agent/sources.rs` is `cfg(test)`-gated at its wrapper in `agent.rs`, and no test with a credential exercises it. The production inspection paths are `ProjectSources` and `read_node`, and both are tested. I do not treat this as a gap against the requirement's text.",
